# Non-secret API routing. Install as /etc/kf/api.env, owned root:kf-api, mode 0640.
LOG_LEVEL=info
OIDC_ISSUER=https://identity.example.internal/realms/knowledge-fabric
OIDC_AUDIENCE=knowledge-fabric-api
OIDC_JWKS_URI=https://identity.example.internal/realms/knowledge-fabric/protocol/openid-connect/certs
# The working store: by default this host's own kf-objects (SeaweedFS on loopback, ADR 0039),
# whose identities provision-host.sh renders; name another S3 store here to use that instead.
S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8333
S3_REGION=us-east-1
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=kf-api
S3_BUCKET_ARTIFACTS=kf-artifacts
S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
# Optional: lets a non-loopback caller read the full GET /readiness report by sending
# X-KF-Readiness-Token. Owner-only file, at least 32 bytes. Without it only a direct loopback
# connection sees the report; everyone else gets the bare verdict.
# KF_READINESS_TOKEN_FILE=/etc/kf/api/readiness-token
# How far back a caller may date an action's effectiveAt (days, default 30), and the action
# types allowed to go further (comma-separated; empty by default). Future times beyond five
# minutes of skew are always refused.
# KF_EFFECTIVE_AT_BACKDATE_DAYS=30
# KF_EFFECTIVE_AT_BACKDATABLE_ACTIONS=
# A person's own urgent-push destination (PUT /notification-destination, 20261011500000): the
# public half of kf-notify's X25519 key (base64url, not a secret; provision-host.sh derives it from
# /etc/kf/notify/destination-key), and the push servers a destination may name, the same list as
# /etc/kf/notify.env. Unset: the route answers 503 and urgent items reach people by the digest.
# KF_NOTIFY_DESTINATION_PUBLIC_KEY=
# KF_NOTIFY_PUSH_SERVERS=https://ntfy.sh
